      "correspondence": "The actual soft baseline is the Gaussian integral of the complete ordered-pair sum with unchanged angle weight lambda and, for the second test, the actual rank-two projected Gaussian norm squared. Nonparallel kernel coarea cancels exactly its inverse Gram factor against lambda. Parallel and diagonal lambda terms are proved zero. Actual fixed-base Gamma and Gaussian integrabilities are proved from uniform density and logistic bounds before finite-sum exchanges. The exact coefficient is h\u00b2/(2 sigma\u00b2) for the ordered hard positive-edge sum, equivalently h\u00b2/sigma\u00b2 for the unordered source ridge sum."
